Package: rsemverse
Type: Package
Title: From RSEM Gene Results to Analysis-Ready Gene Tables
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Turns RSEM '*.genes.results' files into analysis-ready gene
    tables for human and mouse bulk RNA-seq. The files listed in a sample
    table are read into one table of expected counts or TPM with one row per
    gene symbol and one column per sample, using the Bioconductor annotation
    packages 'org.Hs.eg.db' and 'org.Mm.eg.db'. The same table is then
    filtered (the 'edgeR' filterByExpr rule, detection thresholds, most
    variable genes), reduced to built-in gene groups (protein-coding,
    mitochondrial, ribosomal, hemoglobin, sex-chromosome, spike-in),
    normalized between samples (CPM, TMM, upper quartile, DESeq2 median of
    ratios, quantile), transformed (log2, z-score, ranks), and returned as a
    long table with the sample information. No gene list or sample grouping
    is needed, and filtering and normalization give the same results as
    'edgeR', 'DESeq2' and 'limma' without depending on them.
